; Step to the next object, keeping A
;
; Like #R$9B93 but A and BC come back as they went in, so a loop can keep an id
; in A. Only IX, IY and Z are results.
; .
; A Value to keep
; IX Current entry of ObjectTable (or its base minus 3)
; O:IX Next entry
; O:IY Record of the next object
; O:F Z set at the $FF that ends the table
@label=NextObjectKeepA
c$9BA9 PUSH BC       ;
 $9BAA LD B,A        ;
 $9BAB CALL $9B93    ;
 $9BAE LD A,B        ;
 $9BAF POP BC        ;
 $9BB0 RET           ;
